Request to repro:
```javascript
let formData = new FormData();
formData.append('Date', 'John');
fetch("https://localhost:7101/WeatherForecast", {
    body: formData,
    headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
        // "Content-Type": "multipart/form-data",
    },
    method: "post",
});
```

It does look like this is due to a zero-byte read.
If you use the above javascript request it hits the pipe reader code path and generates an empty string output
https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/bec278eabea54f63da15e10e654bdfa4168a2479/src/Http/Http/src/Features/FormFeature.cs#L163
And if you use swagger to generate the form request (and add multipart to MediaTypeOptions) it hits the stream read path
https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/bec278eabea54f63da15e10e654bdfa4168a2479/src/Http/Http/src/Features/FormFeature.cs#L177
Which does generate the expected request body output.

